+### Float utilities
+
+The float key ships whole in the utilities layer from the `src/styles/utilities/_float.scss`
+partial, and the clearfix helper ships beside it from the `src/styles/components/_clearfix.scss`
+partial. The `.float-start`, `.float-end`, and `.float-none` classes set the `float` property at
+every breakpoint infix, so the `.float-md-end` class floats its element to the right from the md
+boundary up. The start side writes the physical `left` value and the end side the physical `right`
+value, as the release writes them, so in a right-to-left scope the `.float-start` class still floats
+a box to the left.
+
+The partial writes the key through the `utility` mixin that § Styles describes and walks the
+breakpoints once, so a wider infix beats every narrower one whatever order the classes are written
+in: at a 768px viewport, an element carrying the `.float-md-end` and `.float-sm-start` classes
+floats to the right. Every declaration carries the `!important` flag the release writes, and none
+reads a token, so neither the density factor nor the color mode moves a value. § Styles shows the
+escape from an important utility inside the utilities layer.
+
+A float leaves its container's height, so a container holding only floats collapses and the content
+after it rises beside them. The `.clearfix` helper writes an empty block after its host's content
+that clears the left and the right side, so the host's height reaches the bottom of its floated
+children. The helper sits in the `components` layer at the release's `_helpers.scss` position, and
+its declarations are normal, as the release writes them, so a rule of your own on the same generated
+box overrides it.
