+### Object fit utilities
+
+The object-fit key ships whole in the utilities layer from the
+`src/styles/utilities/_object-fit.scss` partial. The `.object-fit-contain`, `.object-fit-cover`,
+`.object-fit-fill`, `.object-fit-scale`, and `.object-fit-none` classes set the `object-fit`
+property of a replaced element, such as an image or a video, at every breakpoint infix, and the
+`.object-fit-scale` class writes the `scale-down` value. So a picture drawn at a ratio its box does
+not share is letterboxed by the `contain` value, cropped by the `cover` value, stretched by the
+`fill` value, and kept at its own size by the `none` value; the `scale-down` value keeps the
+picture's own size where the picture fits and letterboxes it where it does not.
+
+The partial writes the key through the `utility` mixin and walks the breakpoints once, so a wider
+infix beats every narrower one: at a 768px viewport, an image carrying the `.object-fit-md-cover`
+and `.object-fit-sm-contain` classes is cropped. Every declaration carries the `!important` flag the
+release writes, and none reads a token.
